==Italian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ML.|ita}} {{term|brunus|brūnus|lang=la}} "brown, brunet" (whence also {{spa}} {{term|bruno|lang=spa}}, {{etyl|fr|-}} {{term|brun|lang=fr}}), of {{etyl|gem|ita}} origin, from {{etyl|frk|ita}} *{{term||brūn|lang=frk}} from {{proto|Germanic|brūnaz|brown|lang=ita}} from {{proto|Indo-European|bher-|shining, brown|lang=ita}}. Akin to {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|brun|brūn|lang=goh}} "brown" ({{de}} {{term|braun|lang=de}} "brown"), {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|brun|brūn|lang=ang}} "brown". More at {{l|en|brown}}.

